Saving Throw: none

When he casts this spell, the warlord must choose the element against which he wishes to create a shield. He can choose fire, cold, electricity or acid. After that, flames rise high around the recipient to protect him, whose nature and color depend on the chosen element. As long as the recipient is covered by this shield, he gets 60% resistance against the chosen element, and any opponent that hits him will suffer 1D6 +3 points of damage from the elemental flames.~
@74661 = ~Elemental Shield (Alteration, Evocation)
Level: 5
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 25 rounds
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

When he casts this spell, the warlord must choose the element against which he wishes to create a shield. He can choose fire, cold, electricity or acid. After that, flames rise high around the recipient to protect him, whose nature and color depend on the chosen element. As long as the recipient is covered by this shield, he gets 60% resistance against the chosen element, and any opponent that hits him will suffer 1D6 +3 points of damage from the elemental flames.

All allies within 5 meters of the recipient also benefit from reduced effects of the spell:
They are protected by a shield that grants 40% resistance against the element and inflicts 1D4 +2 points of damage for 17 rounds.~

@747 = ~Stroke of Luck~
@748 = ~Stroke of Luck (Enchantment)
Level: 4
Range: 0
Duration: 4 rounds
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell grants the warlord a sudden surge of good fortune. The spell grants powerful benefits, but the good fortune quickly fades.
During the first round, he gains a +10 bonus to attack rolls and +2 to the chance to inflict a critical hit, automatically deals maximum damage on a hit plus 1D10 points of magic damage. In addition, he automatically succeeds on all saving throws.
During the second round, he gains a +6 bonus to attack rolls and +1 to the chance to inflict a critical hit, and inflicts the maximum damage +1D8. He also receives a +4 bonus to saving throws.
During the third round, he gains a +3 bonus to attack rolls, +1D6 to damage and +2 to saving throws.
During the last round, he gains a +2 bonus to attack rolls, +1D4 to damage and +1 to saving throws.~
@7481 = ~Stroke of Luck (Enchantment)
Level: 4
Range: 0
Duration: 4 rounds
Casting Time: 2
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell grants the warlord a sudden surge of good fortune. The spell grants powerful benefits, but the good fortune quickly fades.
During the first round, he gains a +10 bonus to attack rolls and +2 to the chance to inflict a critical hit, automatically deals maximum damage on a hit plus 1D10 points of magic damage. In addition, he automatically succeeds on all saving throws.
During the second round, he gains a +6 bonus to attack rolls and +1 to the chance to inflict a critical hit, and inflicts the maximum damage +1D8. He also receives a +4 bonus to saving throws.
During the third round, he gains a +3 bonus to attack rolls, +1D6 to damage and +2 to saving throws.
During the last round, he gains a +2 bonus to attack rolls, +1D4 to damage and +1 to saving throws.~
